    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d82">

                <pb facs="0184" n="146" sameAs="frus:frus1951v03p1/pg146"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.5/4–1751: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The United States Deputy Representative on the North
                        Atlantic Council</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Spofford</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi><anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d82-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">niact</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1951-04-17T14:00:00+01:00">April 17, 1951—2
                            p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p> Depto 791. Todep 366<anchor n="2" xml:id="d82-f2"/> not recd until after mtg
                    reported in Depto 790.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d82-f3"/> However, on basis previous
                    instrs, we insisted and secured agreement upon inclusion of sentence which we
                    believe same in sense and effect as that given in Todep 366. Sentence agreed
                    yesterday read “Deputy shall represent his Government as a whole, particularly
                    those Mins concerned with NATO matters”. Those words make clear each deputy
                    represents all Mins in his Govt concerned with NAT matters and his
                    responsibility to them seems obvious corollary. Agreed sentence spells out first
                    half of sentence in Todep 366 (which is property matter of international
                    concern) and leaves to national determination (as wld last half of suggested
                    sentence) how each govt establishes its lines of direction.</p>
                <p>Strongly hope agreed sentence will be acceptable since final draft incorporating
                    it has been referred to all govts and it wld be highly embarrassing for us to
                    reopen it. Revised agreed minute authorized by Todep 361 and 363<anchor n="4"
                        xml:id="d82-f4"/> adopted with general satisfaction.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Spofford</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d82-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d82-f1-content">
                <p>Repeated to Paris.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d82-f2" n="2" xml:id="d82-f2-content">
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Supra</hi>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d82-f3" n="3" xml:id="d82-f3-content">
                <p>Telegram dated April 17, not printed. It reported on the discussion of various
                    matters in the April 16 meeting of the Council Deputies, including (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">a</hi>) Portugal’s withdrawal of its reservations on the
                    Canadian proposal, (<hi rendition="#italic">b</hi>) the Deputies’ acceptance of
                    the U.S.-Netherlands agreed minute on interpretation of political “guidance,”
                    and (<hi rendition="#italic">c</hi>) the Deputies’ agreement to transmit the
                    approved text of the Canadian proposal to NATO governments with the hope of
                    final action on April 25, if possible incorporating a paragraph on the FEB which
                    would be discussed by the Deputies on April 23 (740.5/4–1750).</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d82-f4" n="4" xml:id="d82-f4-content">
                <p>Neither printed.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
